    "title": "Circle theorems — Class 10 (Sindh Board)",
    "description": "Assalam-o-Alaikum dear students, I have prepared these essential notes on circle theorems to help you excel in your Sindh Board mathematics examinations. It is crucial to grasp that the angle subtended by an arc at the center is twice the angle subtended at the remaining part of the circle, represented by $\\angle AOB = 2\\angle ACB$. Furthermore, always keep in mind that angles in the same segment are equal, such as $\\angle ADB = \\angle ACB$, and that the opposite angles of a cyclic quadrilateral are supplementary, satisfying $\\angle A + \\angle C = 180^\\circ$. Master these fundamental properties to solve complex geometric proofs with confidence.",
